  "description": "Two spacecraft in Sun-synchronous orbits, with follower-1 holding 50 km ahead of chief-1 for 90 days. The chief holds its altitude; the follower mirrors the chief's reboosts and fires small along-track burns when the separation drifts out of tolerance.\n\nWhat to look at:\n- follower-1.phasing_keeping.separation_error and .relative_semi_major_axis.\n- The separation drifts slowly, leaves its 10% band around day 20, and one correction brings it back in about 3 days. It then stays within 48-55 km for ~0.013 m/s.\n\nTry changing:\n- Target separation (a list of values steps through a schedule).\n- Correction window: shorter is faster but costs more delta-V (roughly 1 / window).\n- Tolerance: tighter triggers corrections sooner.\n- follower-1's starting mean anomaly, to begin off target.\n- Duration: under ~20 days no correction fires; the maximum is 100 days.",
  "schema_version": 3
